{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.WeierstrassProjection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.WeierstrassProjection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:QOU.GroundRingCore"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.weierstrass_on_curve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.weierstrass_on_curve","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/WeierstrassProjection.lean#L104-L116","doc":"**The differential equation exhibits `(℘, ℘')` as a point of the\nDescartes elliptic curve** `y² = 4x³ − g₂x − g₃`.\n\nA regression witness for the correction above: this is the content\nthe old existential form *appeared* to provide and did not.  Under\nthat form it was unprovable — `weierstrassProjection` did not occur\nin the axiom, so nothing connected ℘ to the cubic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.weierstrass_diff_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.weierstrass_diff_eq","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/WeierstrassProjection.lean#L95-L102","doc":"The Weierstrass function satisfies the differential equation\n`℘'(z)² = 4℘(z)³ − g₂℘(z) − g₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.weierstrass_diff_eq_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.weierstrass_diff_eq_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/WeierstrassProjection.lean#L59-L93","doc":"**External axiom (Lang, Elliptic Functions Thm VI.3.6):** the\nWeierstrass differential equation\n\n  `℘'(z)² = 4℘(z)³ − g₂·℘(z) − g₃`   for `z ≠ 0`.\n\n**This axiom used to state something else entirely.**  It read\n\n```lean\n∀ (g2 g3 : R_q) (z : ℂ), z ≠ 0 →\n  ∃ (wp_deriv wp_val : ℂ),\n    wp_deriv ^ 2 = 4 * wp_val ^ 3 - coeffEmbed g2 * wp_val - coeffEmbed g3\n```\n\n— an existential over two *free* complex numbers that never mentions\n`weierstrassProjection`.  Over `ℂ` that is a **theorem, not an\naxiom**: take `wp_val := 0` and `wp_deriv` any square root of\n`−g₃`, which exists because `ℂ` is algebraically closed.  Verified by\nproving it outright, `#print axioms` clean\n(`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`).  So the old form\nasserted nothing about ℘, constrained nothing, and its `z` was bound\nbut unused in the conclusion.\n\nThe corrected statement quantifies over the *named* primitives\n`weierstrassProjection` and `weierstrassProjectionDeriv`, which is\nwhat makes it a genuine (and genuinely unproved) external input.\nBean `qou-t7zg`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.weierstrassProjectionDeriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.weierstrassProjectionDeriv","kind":"opaque","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/WeierstrassProjection.lean#L51-L57","doc":"**Derivative `℘'_q` of the Weierstrass projection.**  Opaque for the\nsame reason as `weierstrassProjection` itself: there is no complex\nWeierstrass-℘ in Mathlib to differentiate, so `℘'` enters as its own\nnamed primitive and the differential equation below is what ties the\ntwo together. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.weierstrassProjection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.weierstrassProjection","kind":"opaque","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/WeierstrassProjection.lean#L44-L49","doc":"**External axiom** (Lang, Elliptic Functions §VI.3; manuscript\n§5/weierstrass-projection): the Weierstrass projection ℘_q\nassociated to the Descartes elliptic curve.  Axiomatised pending\na complex Weierstrass-℘ formalisation in Mathlib. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.coeffEmbed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.coeffEmbed","kind":"opaque","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/WeierstrassProjection.lean#L34-L42","doc":"Archimedean specialization map for Laurent-polynomial coefficients.\nThis keeps the formal coefficients in `R_q` while allowing the\ndifferential equation to be stated over `ℂ`.\n\nIntended semantics: a chosen coefficient specialization\n`ℤ[q, q⁻¹] → ℂ` for the archimedean model. The algebraic properties\nof this map are left axiomatic here because this file only needs\ncoefficient transport into the analytic differential equation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}